    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"offset\" part sounds a bit speculative though. If you look at the actual scale of the displacement in places like the Rust Belt or coal country, isn't it more realistic to say that the destruction of existing tax bases and stable industries will fundamentally cripple those local economies before any \"green jobs\" ever show up? It feels like the transition period would be a net negative for stability.",
